  </div>

  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next use:</b> tomorrow, return to the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute retrieval check</a> before you reread the number-and-distance table.</div>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day demonstrative retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Come back tomorrow. Use both the number and the distance cue before you choose.</p>

    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. This marks one near, those marks more than one far, and these marks more than one near; every choice uses both cues.">
      <h3>Choose from memory</h3>
      <p class="choice-hint">Tap each gap, then choose the demonstrative</p>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="This">This</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="That">That</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="These">These</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Those">Those</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="This" data-hint="The laptop is one thing and it is touching the speaker." data-fix="This is my laptop." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is my laptop. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(one · touching you)</span></span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Those" data-hint="Chairs is plural and across the room makes them far." data-fix="Those chairs are available." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> chairs are available. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(more than one · across the room)</span></span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="These" data-hint="Documents is plural and the speaker is holding them." data-fix="These documents are for you." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> documents are for you. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(more than one · in your hand)</span></span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions">
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>

    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="that" data-hint="Bags and are are plural. The bags are also far by the door." data-fix="Those are my bags by the door." data-why="Use those for more than one thing farther away, and pair it with are.">
      <h3>Repair from memory</h3>
      <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
      <p class="ex">That are my bags by the door.</p>
      <div class="spot-options">
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="that">That</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="are">are</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="bags">bags</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="door">door.</button>
      </div>
      <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>

    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Say it without notes</h3>
      <p>Say the new sentence before you reveal it.</p>
      <div class="transform-list">
        <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
          <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> This is my key. → make it plural and keep it near</p>
          <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
          <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>These are my keys.</strong></p>
        </div>
        <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
          <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> These are the offices. → move them far</p>
          <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
          <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Those are the offices.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prompt-card"><b>Thirty-second response:</b> identify one near object, one far object, one near group, and one far group. Use all four demonstratives in complete sentences.</div>
  </section>
